/*
 * zakrefund.mjs
 *
 * Three things the last test order showed were wrong.
 *
 * 1. Paying online said nothing.
 *    "Payment received" hung off Shopify's orders/paid webhook. But an
 *    order this app writes is created already PAID - there is no payment
 *    event for Shopify to announce, so orders/paid never fires and that
 *    message was never sent. The customer paid and heard nothing. It is
 *    now said when the order arrives already settled; if orders/paid does
 *    follow (a Shopify-checkout order) the duplicate is turned away by the
 *    database.
 *
 * 2. Cancelling sent two messages in the same second.
 *    Shopify fires orders/cancelled and refunds/create together, and both
 *    spoke - eight milliseconds apart, so WhatsApp delivered them in
 *    whatever order it liked, refund first. Now only the cancellation
 *    speaks at that moment. It is the news; the refund is not news yet.
 *
 * 3. The refund message was a promise nobody had kept.
 *    An order this app wrote was paid to Razorpay directly, not through
 *    Shopify's own Razorpay gateway. So when it is cancelled Shopify
 *    writes "refunded" against it - but Shopify cannot move that money.
 *    It sits with Razorpay until someone refunds it there by hand. The
 *    customer was being told a refund was on its way when nothing had
 *    left.
 *
 *    Now the app does it. Shopify's refund gives the amount, Razorpay is
 *    asked to send exactly that back, and the customer is told only when
 *    Razorpay reports the money has actually gone - days later, in its own
 *    message. Cancellation first, refund when it is true.
 *
 *    Nothing can send money twice: Razorpay is asked what it has already
 *    refunded before a new refund is made, and the refund id is written
 *    down the moment it exists. A refund the merchant made by hand in the
 *    Razorpay dashboard is adopted rather than duplicated.
 *
 * Every file it touches is copied to ..\zak-bak first, and a file that is
 * not the version this script was built against is left alone and named.
 * Run it from the repo root, after zakretry.mjs.
 */

